[143.857687, "o", "\u001b[?2004huser@c9da50e81b0b:~/infra-configs$ "]
[143.966313, "i", "cat > SECURITY.md << 'EOF'\n# Security Measures for infra-configs Repository\n\n## Git Hooks Protection\n\nThis repository contains sensitive private keys and has multiple layers of protection:\n\n### 1. Pre-commit Hook\n- Checks staged files matching `*.pem` or `*.key` for insecure permissions\n- Blocks commits where private keys have permissions other than 0600 or 0400\n- **WARNING**: Can be bypassed with `git commit --no-verify` (DO NOT USE)\n\n### 2. Pre-push Hook  \n- Scans all commits being pushed for insecure private key permissions\n- Checks the actual file mode stored in git (not just filesystem permissions)\n- Provides a second line of defense if pre-commit was bypassed\n- Cannot be bypassed as easily as pre-commit\n\n### 3. Pre-receive Hook\n- Server-side validation (for bare/remote repositories)\n- Final enforcement point that cannot be bypassed by clients\n\n## How the Previous Breach Occurred\n\nOn commit c149e80 (3 days ago), jenkins-bot committed `secrets/deploy.key` with mode 0644 (world-readable).\n\n**Root Cause**: "]
[143.966425, "i", "The commit was made using `git commit --no-verify` or similar, which bypassed the pre-commit hook.\n\n## Prevention Measures Now in Place\n\n1. **Enhanced pre-commit hook** with clear warnings about --no-verify\n2. **Pre-push hook** that catches bad commits before they reach remote\n3. **Pre-receive hook** for server-side enforcement\n4. **Git configuration**: `hooks.allowNoVerify = false` (advisory)\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### For Developers\n- Always use `chmod 600` on private key files before committing\n- Never use `--no-verify` flag with git commands\n- If hooks block your commit, fix the underlying issue instead of bypassing\n\n### For CI/CD Systems (Jenkins, etc.)\n- Configure automation to respect git hooks\n- Never use `--no-verify` in automated scripts\n- Set proper file permissions before committing\n- Example:\n  ```bash\n  chmod 600 secrets/*.key secrets/*.pem\n  git add secrets/\n  git commit -m \"update keys\"  # No --no-verify!\n  ```\n\n### For Repository Administrators\n- Regularly audit commit history for insecure key f"]
[143.966464, "o", "cat > SECURITY.md << 'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[143.966525, "i", "iles:\n  ```bash\n  git log --all --pretty=format:'%H' | while read commit; do\n    git ls-tree -r $commit | grep -E '\\.(pem|key)$' | grep -v '^100600\\|^100400'\n  done\n  ```\n- Ensure hooks are executable: `chmod +x .git/hooks/pre-*`\n- For remote/bare repos, ensure hooks are installed server-side\n\n## Fixing Existing Bad Commits\n\nIf a commit with insecure permissions is already in history:\n\n1. Fix the file permissions:\n   ```bash\n   chmod 600 secrets/deploy.key\n   ```\n\n2. Stage the corrected file:\n   ```bash\n   git add secrets/deploy.key\n   ```\n\n3. Create a new commit (preferred) or amend:\n   ```bash\n   git commit -m \"fix: correct permissions on deploy.key to 0600\"\n   ```\n\n4. Push the fix:\n   ```bash\n   git push\n   ```\n\n**Note**: Rewriting history (git rebase/filter-branch) is generally not recommended for shared repositories unless absolutely necessary.\n\n## Testing the Hooks\n\nTo verify hooks are working:\n\n```bash\n# Test pre-commit\ntouch test.key\nchmod 644 test.key\ngit add test.key\ngit commit -m \"test\"  # Should b"]
[143.966558, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[143.966602, "i", "e blocked\n\n# Cleanup\ngit reset HEAD test.key\nrm test.key\n```\n\n## Contact\n\nFor security concerns, contact the infrastructure team.\nEOF\n"]
