[220.038672, "i", "cat > INCIDENT_REPORT.md << 'EOF'\n# Security Incident Report: World-Readable Private Key\n\n## Date\nMay 5, 2026\n\n## Summary\nA private key file (secrets/deploy.key) was committed with world-readable permissions (0644) in commit c149e80, bypassing the pre-commit hook.\n\n## Root Cause Analysis\n\n### What Happened\n- Commit c149e80 by jenkins-bot (3 days ago) added secrets/deploy.key with mode 100644\n- The pre-commit hook existed and was functional\n- The hook was bypassed, most likely using `git commit --no-verify`\n\n### Why It Happened\n- Pre-commit hooks can be bypassed with the --no-verify flag\n- Automated systems (jenkins-bot) likely used --no-verify to avoid hook delays\n- No server-side validation was in place to catch bypassed hooks\n- No secondary validation layer existed\n\n### Why It Wasn't Caught\n- Only client-side (pre-commit) validation existed\n- No pre-push hook to catch issues before pushing\n- No server-side (pre-receive) hook for final validation\n\n## Impact\n- One private key file exposed with world-readable "]
[220.038791, "i", "permissions\n- File: secrets/deploy.key\n- Duration: 3 days (from commit until detection)\n\n## Resolution\n\n### Immediate Actions Taken\n1. Fixed file permissions: `chmod 600 secrets/deploy.key`\n2. Committed fix in commit 38b39e6\n\n### Preventive Measures Implemented\n\n#### 1. Enhanced Pre-commit Hook\n- Improved error messages with clear warnings about --no-verify\n- Stricter permission checking (only allows 600 or 400)\n- Location: `.git/hooks/pre-commit`\n\n#### 2. Pre-push Hook (NEW)\n- Validates all commits being pushed for insecure key permissions\n- Checks git object permissions, not just filesystem\n- Provides second layer of defense if pre-commit bypassed\n- Location: `.git/hooks/pre-push`\n- **Cannot be easily bypassed** - runs before push completes\n\n#### 3. Pre-receive Hook (NEW)\n- Server-side validation for bare/remote repositories\n- Final enforcement point that cannot be bypassed by clients\n- Location: `.git/hooks/pre-receive`\n\n#### 4. Git Configuration\n- Set `hooks.allowNoVerify = false` (advisory)\n- Signals int"]
[220.038857, "i", "ent that --no-verify should not be used\n\n#### 5. Documentation\n- Created SECURITY.md with:\n  - Explanation of all protection layers\n  - Best practices for developers and CI/CD\n  - Instructions for fixing issues\n  - Testing procedures\n\n## Testing\n\nValidated that:\n- ✅ Pre-commit hook blocks files with 644 permissions\n- ✅ Pre-commit hook allows files with 600 permissions\n- ✅ Pre-push hook is executable and in place\n- ✅ Pre-receive hook is executable and in place\n- ✅ Current deploy.key has correct 600 permissions\n\n## Recommendations\n\n### For Development Team\n1. Never use `--no-verify` flag in git commands\n2. Always set `chmod 600` on key files before committing\n3. Review SECURITY.md for best practices\n\n### For CI/CD (Jenkins)\n1. Update jenkins-bot scripts to:\n   - Set proper permissions before git operations\n   - Remove any --no-verify flags from git commands\n   - Respect git hooks\n2. Example fix:\n   ```bash\n   chmod 600 secrets/*.key secrets/*.pem\n   git add secrets/\n   git commit -m \"update keys\"  # N"]
[220.038894, "o", "cat > INCIDENT_REPORT.md << 'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[220.038935, "i", "o --no-verify!\n   ```\n\n### For Infrastructure Team\n1. If this repo is pushed to a remote, install hooks there too\n2. For bare repositories, ensure pre-receive hook is active\n3. Consider periodic audits:\n   ```bash\n   git log --all --pretty=format:'%H' | while read commit; do\n     git ls-tree -r $commit | grep -E '\\.(pem|key)$' | grep -v '^100600\\|^100400'\n   done\n   ```\n\n## Lessons Learned\n\n1. **Defense in Depth**: Single-layer protection (pre-commit only) is insufficient\n2. **Client-side hooks are advisory**: They can be bypassed; need server-side enforcement\n3. **Automation needs constraints**: CI/CD systems should respect security hooks\n4. **Documentation matters**: Clear guidance prevents accidental bypasses\n\n## Status\n\n✅ RESOLVED - Multi-layer protection now in place\n\n## Follow-up Actions\n\n- [ ] Update jenkins-bot configuration to remove --no-verify usage\n- [ ] Deploy hooks to remote/bare repository if applicable\n- [ ] Conduct team training on git hook security\n- [ ] Consider rotating the exposed deplo"]
[220.038968, "o", "ent that --no-verify should not be used\r\n\r\n#### 5. Documentation\r\n- Created SECURITY.md with:\r\n  - Explanation of all protection layers\r\n  - Best practices for developers and CI/CD\r\n  - Instructions for fixing issues\r\n  "]
